### 🟩 Core Lifecycle & Enforcement Functions

| **Function**                              | **Description**                                                                                                   |
| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Mint Unit™**                            | Unique, single-cause digital object. One unit = one intent, one action, one lifecycle.                            |
| **Validate-on-Action**                    | Validation occurs at the point of interaction (scan, time, GPS, device). No external runtime needed.              |
| **Burn-on-Use**                           | After validation, unit self-destructs to prevent reuse, spoofing, or unauthorized duplication.                    |
| **Lifecycle Expiry / TTL**                | Units expire based on embedded logic: time, use, location, or condition.                                          |
| **Shepherd Coin™ Generation**             | Upon successful use and burn, a cryptographic proof token is minted to signal completed lifecycle.                |
| **Proof-of-Intent**                       | Each unit embeds a traceable causal origin — e.g., voter intent, event entry, credential grant.                   |
| **Offline Capability**                    | Logic executes locally — validation can occur without cloud or blockchain dependencies.                           |
| **Tamper Detection / Self-Destruct**      | Units trigger burn if tampered with or used in an invalid context (wrong device, IP, etc.).                       |
| **Reflexive Governance Hooks**            | Data governance and behavioral enforcement embedded in the token, not external to it (RBGA-compatible).           |
| **Causal Chain Auditing**                 | Full lifecycle — from mint to validation to burn — is audit-ready and timestamp-anchored.                         |
| **Credential Lifecycle Enforcement**      | Prevents session hijack, double-use, and credential drift by enforcing expiration and proof-on-use.               |
| **Token-Triggered Rights**                | Token usage grants a limited permission or action — if unused or misused, no rights activate.                     |
| **Multi-Layered Validation Gates**        | Allows logic to reference multiple contextual triggers (e.g., time, GPS, authority scope) before granting access. |
| **Non-Repudiation via Burned State**      | Once used, token becomes unforgeable proof of action; no one can deny or spoof its use.                           |
| **Behavioral Data Logic**                 | Lifecycle units can evolve based on user behavior and trigger different outcomes.                                 |
| **Portability Across Legacy and Quantum** | Logic native to device level makes this future-proof across computing paradigms.                                  |
| **Relic-Based Tokenization**              | Burned Mint Units leave immutable proof artifacts — the basis of digital relic vaulting (e.g., Shepherd Coin).    |
| **Use-of-Use Finalization**               | Every token or action resolves into a final state — nothing is left open-ended or dangling.                       |
| **Hybrid Paper + Digital Sync**           | In voting, each Mint Unit maps directly to a real-world physical ballot — zero duplication possible.              |
| **Credential Mutation Control**           | Credentials mutate based on valid completion cycles, not arbitrary backend decisions.                             |

